      "source": [
        "## BONUS: `if __name__ == 'main'`\n",
        "\n",
        "If you head to the folder in sample_code, you may notice a funny line:\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1-8,focus:9,dim:10-13\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "class Animation:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, event_log):\n",
        "        ...\n",
        "\n",
        "    def build_animation(self, time_interval=1):\n",
        "        return animate_activity_log(event_log=self.event_log,\n",
        "            event_position_df=self.layout, every_x_time_units=time_interval)\n",
        "\n",
        "if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n",
        "    my_params = Param()\n",
        "    my_model = Model(my_params)\n",
        "    my_model.run_model()\n",
        "    ...\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## BONUS: `if __name__ == 'main'` - explanation\n",
        "\n",
        "`if __name__ == 'main':` simply means [**'only run the code in this block if you are running the original file'**]{style=\"color:yellow\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "When you run the file (script) in the terminal or the interactive window, the code in this block will run (execute).\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.fragment}\n",
        "HOWEVER, if you import pieces of that code into another file, it *won't* run the bit in the `if __name__ == 'main':` block.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.value-box fragment=\"fade-in\" icon=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\" icon-position=\"left\" align=\"center\" color=\"bg-green\"}\n",
        "This is really useful if we want to reuse our classes somewhere else, like in a web app, so we'll be getting in the habit of doing this.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Advanced Vidigi Elements: Resources\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why is Resource Use Different to Queues?\n",
        "\n",
        "So far, we've used a queue for resource use\n",
        "\n",
        "And this works, but has a couple of downsides\n",
        "\n",
        "- People move through the resource use step like a queue rather than staying with a single resource\n",
        "- You can't see resources that **aren't** being used, so it's difficult to tell whether the system is underutilising resources\n",
        "\n",
        "(you can usually tell if it's *over* capacity because a queue will be building up!)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## What do we change?\n",
        "\n",
        "We don't have to change too much\n",
        "\n",
        "1. We will swap in a *custom* resource class instead of Simpy.Resource\n",
        "1. We will capture the ID of the resource used\n",
        "1. We will swap the logging type for resource use events and store this resource ID\n",
        "1. We will pass our params class to our animation (so it knows how many resources there are) and our event position dataframe.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Custom Resource Classes\n",
        "\n",
        "Vidigi provides two key custom resource classes\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "::: {.value-box align=\"center\" value=\"VidigiStore\"}\n",
        "Equivalent to `simpy.Resource`\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "::: {.value-box align=\"center\" value=\"VidigiPriorityStore\"}\n",
        "Equivalent to `simpy.PriorityResource`\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.value-box icon=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" icon-position=\"left\" color=\"bg-red\"}\n",
        "We don't want to use *VidigiResource*.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is a special class that Vidigi uses internally, and by itself it won't allow us to track the resource\n",
        "ID in the way we need to.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why do we need these?\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's imagine we have two nurses.\n",
        "\n",
        "SimPy resources don't *really* have a concept of separate nurses behind the scenes.\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 60vh\">\n",
        "\n",
        "<img src=\"../diagrams/SimpyResource.drawio.svg\" style=\"height: 60vh;\">\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "## The VidigiStore approach\n",
        "\n",
        "In contrast, a VidigiStore is filled with individual nurses, each with their own ID.\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 60vh\">\n",
        "\n",
        "<img src=\"../diagrams/VidigiStore.drawio.svg\" style=\"height: 60vh;\">\n",
        "\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "If vidigi knows the ID of a resource, it ensures that people are assigned to the right resource in the animation for the whole time they are using it.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Adding Resource Use to Vidigi Animations\n",
        "\n",
        "To recap, we're going to\n",
        "\n",
        "1. swap in a *custom* resource class instead of Simpy.Resource\n",
        "1. capture the ID of the resource used\n",
        "1. swap the logging type for resource use events and store this resource ID\n",
        "1. pass our params class to our animation (so it knows how many resources there are) and our event position dataframe.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1a. Import the new resource class\n",
        "\n",
        "First, we need to make sure we have imported our new class.\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "from vidigi.resources import VidigiStore\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.value-box value=\"Note\" icon=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\" icon-position=\"left\" align=\"center\" color=\"bg-green\"}\n",
        "We *could* instead use\n",
        "\n",
        "`import vidigi`\n",
        "\n",
        "And then\n",
        "\n",
        "`vidigi.resources.VidigiStore`\n",
        "\n",
        "whenever we want to use it, but the vidigi documentation uses the convention detailed above\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1b. Swap in the new resource class instead of Simpy.Resource\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Before\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1-3,focus:4\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "class Model:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, param):\n",
        "        ...\n",
        "        self.nurse = simpy.Resource(self.env, capacity=self.param.num_nurses)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "#### After\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1-3,focus:4\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "class Model:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, param):\n",
        "        ...\n",
        "        self.nurse = VidigiStore(self.env, num_resources=self.param.num_nurses) # UPDATED\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style='font-size: 75%;'}\n",
        "- We change `simpy.Resource` to `VidigiStore`\n",
        "- We change 'capacity' to 'num_resources' (as capacity has its own special meaning in vidigi's resources)\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## 2. Capture the ID of the resource\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Before\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1-4,focus:5-6\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "def attend_clinic(self, patient):\n",
        "        ...\n",
        "        self.logger.log_queue(entity_id=patient.id, event=\"nurse_wait_begins\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        with self.nurse.request() as req:\n",
        "            yield req\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "#### After\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1-4,focus:5-6\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "def attend_clinic(self, patient):\n",
        "        ...\n",
        "        self.logger.log_queue(entity_id=patient.id, event=\"nurse_wait_begins\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        with self.nurse.request() as req:\n",
        "            nurse_obtained = yield req # UPDATED\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style=\"font-size: 70%;\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "We need to assign the result of this yield to a variable. We'll then be able to extract the resource ID for logging.\n",
        "\n",
        "We can call it anything, but make sure you don't name it the exact same thing as your resource!\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## 3a. Swap the logging type\n",
        "\n",
        "we will swap the logging type from `log_queue` to `log_resource_use_start` and `log_resource_use_end`\n",
        "\n",
        "These methods accept an extra parameter - `resource_id`.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='40%'}\n",
        "### Before\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "self.logger.log_queue(\n",
        "    entity_id=patient.id,\n",
        "    event=\"being_seen_by_nurse\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "```\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='60%'}\n",
        "### After\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"focus:1,dim:2-3,focus:4,dim:5\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "self.logger.log_resource_use_start( # UPDATED\n",
        "    entity_id=patient.id,\n",
        "    event=\"being_seen_by_nurse\",\n",
        "    resource_id=nurse_obtained.id_attribute,  # NEW\n",
        ")\n",
        "```\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "The variable we assigned to is a VidigiResource object behind the scenes, and that has a special `id_attribute` we can access that contains a unique identifier for that resource.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 3b. Repeat this for when they finish with the resource\n",
        "\n",
        "Just before the end of the indented nurse block, we do this to record in our event log that the resource  became free at that point.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='40%'}\n",
        "### Before\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "self.logger.log_queue(\n",
        "    entity_id=patient.id,\n",
        "    event=\"nurse_treatment_ends\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "```\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='60%'}\n",
        "### After\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"focus:1,dim:2-3,focus:4,dim:5\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "self.logger.log_resource_use_end( # UPDATED\n",
        "    entity_id=patient.id,\n",
        "    event=\"nurse_treatment_ends\",\n",
        "    resource_id=nurse_obtained.id_attribute,  # NEW\n",
        ")\n",
        "```\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## SUMMARY: our full revised `attend_clinic()` method\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1-6,focus:7,dim:8-11,focus:12-15,dim:16-19,focus:20-23,dim:24-25\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "def attend_clinic(self, patient):\n",
        "    self.logger.log_arrival(entity_id=patient.id)\n",
        "    start_q_nurse = self.env.now\n",
        "    self.logger.log_queue(entity_id=patient.id, event=\"nurse_wait_begins\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    with self.nurse.request() as req:\n",
        "        nurse_obtained = yield req # UPDATED\n",
        "\n",
        "        end_q_nurse = self.env.now\n",
        "        patient.q_time_nurse = end_q_nurse - start_q_nurse\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.logger.log_resource_use_start( # UPDATED\n",
        "            entity_id=patient.id, event=\"being_seen_by_nurse\",\n",
        "            resource_id=nurse_obtained.id_attribute, # NEW\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        sampled_nurse_act_time = self.nurse_consult_time_dist.sample()\n",
        "        yield self.env.timeout(sampled_nurse_act_time)\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.logger.log_resource_use_end( # UPDATED\n",
        "            entity_id=patient.id, event=\"nurse_treatment_ends\",\n",
        "            resource_id=nurse_obtained.id_attribute # NEW\n",
        "            )\n",
        "\n",
        "    self.logger.log_departure(entity_id=patient.id)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## 4. Pass our params class to our animation class...\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "class Animation:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, event_log, params):  # UPDATED\n",
        "        self.event_log = event_log\n",
        "        self.params = params  # NEW\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "And, when we call it later\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "my_animation = Animation(my_params, my_event_log)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## 4b. ... our event position df...\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1-3,focus:4-7,dim:8\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "self.layout = create_event_position_df(\n",
        "    [EventPosition(event=\"arrival\", x=0, y=350, label=\"Entrance\"),\n",
        "     EventPosition(event=\"nurse_wait_begins\", x=200, y=250, label=\"Waiting for Nurse\"),\n",
        "     EventPosition(\n",
        "        event=\"being_seen_by_nurse\", x=200, y=150, label=\"Being Seen By Nurse\",\n",
        "        resource=\"num_nurses\", # NEW\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    EventPosition(event=\"depart\", x=200, y=50, label=\"Exit\")])\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='35%'}\n",
        "::: {style='font-size: 70%;'}\n",
        "When we pass the resource name, this will be looked up from our Params class, so we need to make sure the name exactly matches how it's written there\n",
        "\n",
        "We **still** don't need to visualise the 'nurse_treatment_ends' step!\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='65%'}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1-8,focus:9,dim:10-11\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "class Param:\n",
        "  def __init__(\n",
        "      self, ...\n",
        "      sd_nurse_consult_time=1, num_nurses=1,\n",
        "      sim_duration=120, ...\n",
        "  ):\n",
        "      ...\n",
        "      self.sd_nurse_consult_time = sd_nurse_consult_time\n",
        "      self.num_nurses = num_nurses\n",
        "      self.sim_duration = sim_duration\n",
        "      ...\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## 4c. ... and our animation method\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1-5,focus:6,dim:7\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "def build_animation(self, time_interval=1):\n",
        "    return animate_activity_log(\n",
        "        event_log=self.event_log,\n",
        "        event_position_df=self.layout,\n",
        "        every_x_time_units=time_interval,\n",
        "        scenario=self.params,  # NEW\n",
        "    )\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## The event log\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {style='font-size: 75%;'}\n",
        "Our event log now has a new `resource_id` column.\n",
        ":::\n"
      ],
