        "\n",
        "# Incorporating the Trial Class\n",
        "\n",
        "## Trial, trial again\n",
        "\n",
        "So far we've been working with a vidigi model that only runs a single replication.\n",
        "\n",
        "However, we saw in earlier sessions how important it is to run **multiple replications** in simulation.\n",
        "\n",
        "So how can we make vidigi play nicely with the trial class?\n",
        "\n",
        "## Recapping the Trial Class\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "class Trial:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, param):\n",
        "        self.param = param\n",
        "        self.list_of_simulation_replications = []\n",
        "        self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.trial_sd_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "\n",
        "    def run_trial(self):\n",
        "        for replication_id in range(self.param.num_replications):\n",
        "            model_replication = Model(self.param)\n",
        "            model_replication.run_model()\n",
        "            patient_df = model_replication.convert_entity_list_to_dataframe(\n",
        "                model_replication.list_of_patients\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            model_replication.calculate_run_results(patient_df)\n",
        "            self.list_of_simulation_replications.append(model_replication)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def calculate_trial_results(self):\n",
        "        self.replication_df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "            replication.__dict__ for replication in self.list_of_simulation_replications\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse = self.replication_df[\"mean_q_time_nurse\"].mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.trial_sd_q_time_nurse = self.replication_df[\"mean_q_time_nurse\"].std()\n",
        "\n",
        "        self.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse = self.replication_df[\n",
        "            \"mean_q_time_nurse\"\n",
        "        ].quantile(0.9)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tracking Replications - Tweaking the Model Class\n",
        "\n",
        "Vidigi works best if it knows what run a trial came from.\n",
        "\n",
        "So first we're going to go and tweak our `Model` class to store the run number and pass it to our EventLogger.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"dim:1,focus:2,dim:3,focus:4,dim:5-7\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "class Model:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, param, run_number): # UPDATED\n",
        "        self.param = param\n",
        "        self.run_number = run_number  # NEW\n",
        "        self.env = simpy.Environment()\n",
        "        self.patient_counter = 0\n",
        "        ...\n",
        "        self.logger = EventLogger(env=self.env, run_number=self.run_number) # UPDATED\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tracking Replications - Adding a new attribute\n",
        "\n",
        "We're going to be making use of Vidigi's `TrialLogger` class.\n",
        "\n",
        "This takes multiple EventLogger objects and allows us to do fancy things with them!\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "First, we update our import statement\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='50%'}\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "from vidigi.logging import EventLogger, TrialLogger # UPDATED\n",
        "```\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='40%'}\n",
        "Next, we need to update our `__init__` method to set up an attribute to store this object in.\n",
        "\n",
        "We initialise an empty TrialLogger so we can add our EventLogger objects to it as we go.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width='60%'}\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"focus:1-2,dim:3-7,focus:8\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "class Trial:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, param):\n",
        "        self.param = param\n",
        "        self.list_of_simulation_replications = []\n",
        "        self.trial_mean_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.trial_sd_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.trial_perc_90_q_time_nurse = pd.NA\n",
        "        self.trial_logger = TrialLogger()  # NEW\n",
        "```\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tracking Replications - Tweaking the Trial Class\n",
        "\n",
        "We now just pass our replication_id into the model in the `run_trial()` method.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python code-line-style=\"focus:1-3,dim:4-9,focus:10\" code-line-style-preset=\"emphasis\"}\n",
        "def run_trial(self):\n",
        "    for replication_id in range(self.param.num_replications):\n",
        "        model_replication = Model(self.param, replication_id) # UPDATED\n",
        "        model_replication.run_model()\n",
        "        patient_df = model_replication.convert_entity_list_to_dataframe(\n",
        "            model_replication.list_of_patients\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        model_replication.calculate_run_results(patient_df)\n",
        "        self.list_of_simulation_replications.append(model_replication)\n",
        "        self.trial_logger.add_log(model_replication.logger) # NEW\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.value-box fragment=\"fade-in\" icon=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" icon-position=\"left\" align=\"center\" color=\"bg-amber\"}\n",
        "Note that the replication_id will count from 0\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Getting a run from the TrialLogger\n",
        "\n",
        "Now we need to update our code to grab an event log for animation.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Before\n",
        "\n",
        "```{.python}\n",
        "my_event_log = my_model.get_vidigi_event_log()\n",
